{"book":"integers","bookTitle":"Integers","concept":4,"title":"Subtracting integers","grades":"Grade 7","goal":"I can subtract integers, including subtracting a negative number.","teach":"Subtracting a positive number moves you left. Subtracting a <b>negative</b> number is the same as adding its opposite: 5 − (−3) = 5 + 3 = 8. The <b>difference</b> between two numbers is the distance between them on a number line.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:702px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 104\"><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"500\" y2=\"60\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">−4</text><line x1=\"86.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"86.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"86.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">−3</text><line x1=\"132.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"132.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"132.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">−2</text><line x1=\"178.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"178.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">−1</text><line x1=\"224.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"224.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"224.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">0</text><line x1=\"270.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"270.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"270.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">1</text><line x1=\"316.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"316.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"316.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">2</text><line x1=\"362.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"362.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"362.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">3</text><line x1=\"408.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"408.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"408.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">4</text><line x1=\"454.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"454.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"454.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">5</text><line x1=\"500.0\" y1=\"52\" x2=\"500.0\" y2=\"68\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.1\"/><text x=\"500.0\" y=\"85.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#444444\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">6</text><circle cx=\"86.0\" cy=\"60\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#7A0000\"/><circle cx=\"454.0\" cy=\"60\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#7A0000\"/><path d=\"M86.0,57 Q270.0,-3.0 454.0,57\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M447.0,50 L454.0,57 L452.9,48\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><text x=\"270.0\" y=\"21.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\">8 steps</text></svg></span><div class=\"cap\">The distance from −3 to 5 is 8, so 5 − (−3) = 8.</div></div>","ex":{"q":"Calculate −2 − 6 and −2 − (−6).","steps":["−2 − 6: start at −2 and move 6 to the left: −8.","−2 − (−6): subtracting −6 is the same as adding 6.","−2 + 6 = 4."]},"watch":"Two minus signs next to each other, − (−6), become + 6. But − (+6) stays − 6.","qs":[{"text":"Calculate −3 − 8.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"-11","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Move 8 left from −3.","steps":"1. Rule (subtracting integers): subtracting a number is the same as adding its opposite: a − b = a + (−b), so a − (−b) = a + b.<br>2. −3 − 8 = −3 + (−8)<br>3. = −11"},{"text":"Calculate 6 − 15.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"-9","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"Move 15 left from 6.","steps":"1. Rule (subtracting integers): subtracting a number is the same as adding its opposite: a − b = a + (−b), so a − (−b) = a + b.<br>2. 6 − 15 = 6 + (−15)<br>3. Different signs: 15 − 6 = 9; 15 is the bigger size and it is negative.<br>4. 6 − 15 = −9"},{"text":"Calculate −10 − (−4).","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Answer","a":"-6","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"−10 + 4","steps":"1. Rule (subtracting integers): subtracting a number is the same as adding its opposite: a − b = a + (−b), so a − (−b) = a + b.<br>2. −10 − (−4) = −10 + 4<br>3. = −6"}]}